    {
      "name": "Shell Spin Attack",
      "type": "feat",
      "img": "icons/creatures/reptiles/turtle-shell-glowing-green.webp",
      "system": {
        "description": {
          "value": "<p>A Koopa Troopa can withdraw into its shell and launch itself at an enemy as a spinning projectile, sliding across the ground in a straight line up to 20 feet. One creature in the path must make a DC 12 Dexterity saving throw, taking 2d6 bludgeoning damage on a failure or half on a success. After the spin, the Troopa emerges from its shell in the space at the end of the movement, prone, and cannot take reactions until the start of its next turn.</p><p>The shell spin is the Troop's signature combat technique—every recruit learns it during basic training, practices it until the timing is automatic, and uses it in combat with the specific commitment of someone who knows that turning yourself into a projectile has inherent risks but also knows that the alternative is being stomped by something larger than you.</p>",
          "chat": "<p>The shell spins across the ground with the commitment of someone who has accepted that being a living cannonball is part of the job description.</p>"
        },
