    {
      "name": "Kamek's Orders (Current Concern)",
      "type": "feat",
      "img": "icons/skills/social/diplomacy-handshake-yellow.webp",
      "system": {
        "description": {
          "value": "<p>Koopa Troopas currently serve under Kamek's consolidated command following Bowser's extended absence. They follow orders because the chain of command requires it, but growing unease about Kamek's priorities—consolidation over rescue, control over search—has created a morale situation that could be exploited by parties who understand koopa loyalty structures.</p><p>Koopa Troopas who learn that Bowser is alive and that someone is actively trying to reach him become significantly more sympathetic to that someone's cause. A DC 13 Charisma (Persuasion) check can convince a Troopa to share information about Kamek's operations, patrol schedules, or defensive positions if the party demonstrates genuine intent to help Bowser. A DC 16 check can convince a Troopa to actively assist, though the assistance will be limited by the Troopa's fear of Kamek's magical capabilities.</p><p>Koopas who served directly under Bowser—veterans who remember his personal leadership rather than Kamek's proxy authority—are easier to turn (DC reduces by 3) because their loyalty is to the king rather than the institution.</p>",
          "chat": "<p>They follow Kamek because the rules say follow Kamek. They'd follow Bowser because their hearts say follow Bowser. The gap between rules and hearts is where opportunities live.</p>"
        },
